  "task_assistant_messages": [
    "Let \\(f\\) be the number of football players in Mr. Roper’s class.\n\nThe percentage of football players is\n\n\\[\n\\frac{f}{32}\\times 100\\%.\n\\]\n\nSince the number \\(f\\) of football players is not provided, the percentage **cannot be determined** from the given information.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Cannot be determined}}\n\\]",
    "Knowing that the class has 30 students is not enough to determine the percentage. We also need the number of football players.\n\nIf \\(f\\) students are football players, then\n\n\\[\n\\text{percentage}=\\frac{f}{30}\\times 100\\%.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Cannot be determined without the number of football players}}\n\\]",
    "The problem states that \\(25\\%\\) of Mr. Roper’s class are football players.\n\nTherefore, the percentage is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25\\%}\n\\]\n\n(With 30 students, \\(25\\%\\) would correspond to \\(7.5\\) students, so the numbers are not consistent with a whole number of students.)",
    "We are told that \\(20\\%\\) of Mr. Roper’s class are football players.\n\nWith 30 students:\n\n\\[\n0.20 \\times 30 = 6\n\\]\n\nSo 6 students are football players, which is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{20\\%}\n\\]",
